{
 "labview": "LabVIEW 2026 Community 26.3.1f1 (Windows x64)",
 "captured": "2026-10-14",
 "method": "LabVIEW driven through its ActiveX server (LabVIEW.Application) from Python with pywin32. VI Scripting is not reachable over ActiveX, so the test VIs were made from a copy of the shipped example examples/Booleans/Boolean Functions.vi by editing its block diagram heap with pylabview: one node replaced by the Boolean Array To Number (or Number To Boolean Array) primitive, the output representation and Sign Extension Mode set, the VI re-created. LabVIEW loaded, type-propagated, compiled and ran each VI; inputs were set and outputs read over ActiveX, so every output value is LabVIEW's.",
 "boolean_array_to_number.json": "30 configurations: node output U8, U16, U32, U64, I8, I16, I32, I64 set explicitly, each under the three Sign Extension Mode settings, plus 6 with no explicit output representation (the node's default, read into an I64 and a U64 indicator). Arrays of lengths 0, 1, 2, 3, 7, 8, 9, 15, 16, 17, 31, 32, 33, 63, 64 and 65: all FALSE, all TRUE, alternating both ways and 3 seeded random arrays (seed 20261014); duplicate inputs dropped. Re-encoded compactly from the capture records listed in sources.",
 "number_to_boolean_array.json": "8 integer types: minimum, maximum, -1, 0, 1 and seeded values; each input was read back unchanged from the control before the run.",
 "datalog_bool_len*.dat": "front-panel datalog files LabVIEW wrote (LogFilePath + LogAtFinish) for a copy of the same example after Input Array X was set; copied unchanged. Input Array X, element 0 first, per file: {\"datalog_bool_len0.dat\": \"\", \"datalog_bool_len1.dat\": \"1\", \"datalog_bool_len8.dat\": \"10110010\", \"datalog_bool_len9.dat\": \"010011011\", \"datalog_bool_len17.dat\": \"01000110001111100\", \"datalog_bool_len300.dat\": \"\"}",
